1. Project Summary

TENTORA is an AI-powered creative-solutions platform that connects project needs, ready interactive design, visual taste, and human creative expertise in one organized experience.

The platform gives project owners two connected paths:

Design Now: choose a ready interactive design, customize approved properties quickly, and preview, save, or export the result.

Work With a Creative: select one or multiple services, complete one visual taste test, receive up to six compatible creative or team recommendations, select the preferred option, and manage the project through delivery.

TENTORA is not a conventional freelance marketplace, a generic template catalogue, or a blank-canvas AI generator. It is designed to shorten the route from creative need to usable result while preserving human authorship and professional execution.

Important: This closure document must describe verified implementation only. Replace all Pending, TBD, and bracketed fields with real evidence after Stage 4. Do not mark a feature complete because it was planned.

2. Problem Addressed

Project owners often spend significant time browsing portfolios, moving between platforms, and trying to identify creatives who understand both the required service and the desired visual direction.

The problem becomes more complex when one project requires several services. Separate searches may produce disconnected creative work, repeated onboarding, inconsistent styles, and difficult project coordination.

TENTORA addresses this fragmentation by:

Organizing discovery by project sector and service.

Showing services through real visual work.

Providing an immediate Ready Design path for urgent needs.

Using one Main Taste Profile across a multi-service project.

Limiting recommendations to a small, relevant set.

Supporting a creative or visually compatible team.

Connecting self-service work to professional execution.

Keeping custom projects organized through delivery.

3. Final Product Experience

3.1 Shared Entry

Sector → Service → Choose Product Path

3.2 Design Now

Sector → Service → Ready Interactive Design → Customize → Preview → Save or Export

The user begins with a ready structured design rather than a blank canvas. Editable properties and AI-assisted actions remain inside the limits defined by the original design.

3.3 Work With a Creative

Sector → Services and Work → My Project Needs → One Taste Test → Optional Service Direction → Up to Six Recommendations → Selection → Workspace → Delivery

3.4 Connected Handoff

Saved Ready Design → Continue With a Creative → Transfer Design Context → Professional Development

The final closure review must verify each implemented journey against the Stage 4 test evidence.

