14. Lessons Learned

Complete this section after the final retrospective.

14.1 Product Lessons

Did users understand the difference between Design Now and Work With a Creative?

Were Ready Designs faster than starting a custom project?

Which editable properties caused confusion?

Did one Main Taste Profile work across several services?

Were six recommendations enough, too many, or too few?

Did users understand why creatives or teams were recommended?

Was the handoff to a creative valuable and clear?

14.2 Technical Lessons

Which renderer was most suitable for the pilot designs?

Which AI actions added measurable value?

Which actions should remain deterministic rather than AI-based?

Was the modular-monolith structure effective for the team?

Were the Taste Profile and Creative DNA schemas flexible enough?

Did progressive authentication preserve anonymous progress reliably?

Which integrations created the most risk or delay?

14.3 Process Lessons

Were responsibilities clear from the first sprint?

Was QA involved before implementation rather than only after it?

Were API contracts documented before frontend integration?

Was deployment tested early enough?

Were rights and licence reviews part of the feature workflow?

Did the team collect evidence continuously?

